/*!
\page page_stmtdcollection StMtdCollection — Collection Documentation

\section mtd_overview Overview

\ref StMtdCollection is the event-level container for data from the
<b>Muon Telescope Detector (MTD)</b>.  The MTD is an array of MRPC modules
mounted on the outside of the STAR magnet return yoke at mid-rapidity,
identifying muons by detecting penetrating particles beyond the magnet steel.
It enables measurements of di-muon resonances (J/ψ, Υ) and open heavy-flavour
decays.

The collection holds reconstructed hits (\ref StMtdHit), raw TDC hits
(\ref StMtdRawHit), and an event-wise header (\ref StMtdHeader).
\ref StMtdPidTraits live on the associated track, not here.

\section mtd_ownership Object Ownership

- <b>mMtdHeader</b> (\ref StMtdHeader*): Owned. Assigned via \c setHeader() and
  <b>deleted by the destructor</b>.
- <b>mMtdHits</b> (\c StSPtrVecMtdHit): Owned; elements deleted by \c StSPtrVec.
- <b>mMtdRawHits</b> (\c StSPtrVecMtdRawHit): Owned; same semantics.
- The collection itself is owned by the \c StEvent framework.

\section mtd_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \ref StMtdHeader* | mMtdHeader | Event-wise MTD header: fiber header/trigger words, TPC sector mask, quality flags. Owned and deleted by this class. |
| \c StSPtrVecMtdHit | mMtdHits | Reconstructed \ref StMtdHit objects (backleg 1–30, module 1–5, cell, leading/trailing edges, ToT, calibrated tof). |
| \c StSPtrVecMtdRawHit | mMtdRawHits | Raw TDC \ref StMtdRawHit objects from the DAQ stream (fiber ID, backleg, channel, TDC count). |

\section mtd_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c mtdHeader() | Pointer to the MTD event header (mutable and const overloads). |
| \c mtdHits() | Reference to the reconstructed hit collection. |
| \c mtdRawHits() | Reference to the raw TDC hit collection. |
| \c setHeader(StMtdHeader*) | Assigns the header; collection takes ownership. |
| \c addHit(const StMtdHit*) | Appends a reconstructed hit (null-safe). |
| \c addRawHit(const StMtdRawHit*) | Appends a raw hit (null-safe). |
| \c hitsPresent() const | Returns \c true if the hit collection is non-empty. |
| \c rawHitsPresent() const | Returns \c true if the raw hit collection is non-empty. |
| \c IsFolder() const | Returns \c true; enables folder display in a ROOT \c TBrowser. |
| \c Browse(TBrowser*) | Populates a \c TBrowser with the hit and raw-hit collections. |

\section mtd_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StMtdCollection* mtdColl = event->mtdCollection();
if (!mtdColl) return;

if (mtdColl->hitsPresent()) {
    const StSPtrVecMtdHit& hits = mtdColl->mtdHits();
    for (size_t i = 0; i < hits.size(); ++i) {
        StMtdHit* hit = hits[i];
        int backleg = hit->backleg();  // 1-30
        int module  = hit->module();   // 1-5
        double tof  = hit->tof();      // calibrated [ns]
    }
}
\endcode

\see StMtdHit, StMtdRawHit, StMtdHeader
*/
